 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Sure, complementary color is any color its contrast with its complement makes stronger. For example, blue and yellow paints are complementary because they are on opposite ends of the color wheel. It matters because using a yellow against a blue background makes the yellow pop and the blue look deep. In some cases, yes. If you want to make a green shadow, you'd use green paper against a bright light, yellow against dark, or white. You' save bit of money too. A small pack of it goes a long way.",
